    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm looking into a zoning issue for a client in Austin. We have a parcel currently zoned R-1 (Single-Family Residential) that we want to reclassify to Mixed-Use. However, we've run into some conflicting language in the municipal code regarding setback requirements and existing encroachments from the neighboring commercial lot. Can you help me outline a strategy for navigating these conflicting clauses during the rezoning application process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For conflicting zoning code language, your initial strategy should be to request a formal clarification or interpretation from the City of Austin Planning Department. You should also compile a detailed map clearly illustrating where the existing encroachments fall in relation to the current R-1 setbacks versus the proposed Mixed-Use setbacks. Presenting a robust justification detailing the unique circumstances of the property will help the reviewers understand why a deviation or specific interpretation is necessary for a successful rezoning.",
